<title>CHINA: China constructs cobalt oxide plant in Hainan.</title>
<headline>China constructs cobalt oxide plant in Hainan.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>China has begun construction of a production line for cobalt oxide in the southern province of Hainan with investment of 73 million yuan, the Xinhua news agency said.</p>
<p>The line is expected to produce 200 tonnes of cobalt oxide a year, or 12 percent of China's total, after completion, Xinhua said in an overnight report.</p>
<p>The project was likely to become the backbone of southern Hainan province's non-ferrous metal smelting industry, with an estimated output value of 178 million yuan, Xinhua said.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
</text>
